# Close terminals and free ports

Before the final reply, stop processes **you** started in this chat. Closing a terminal pane is not enough; child Node processes can keep the port.

| Service | Port |
|---|---|
| API (Express) | **3002** |
| Admin Vite (`admin/`) | **5173** |
| Client Vite (`client/`) | **5174** |

Free a port **only** when **your** process (or an orphan from this chat) still holds it. Never kill a listener the user already had running. Occupied port ≠ permission to stop it — see `reuse-existing-dev-servers`.

```powershell
# Only for PIDs this chat started — never blanket-kill these ports
Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort <port> -State Listen -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |
  Select-Object -ExpandProperty OwningProcess -Unique |
  ForEach-Object { Stop-Process -Id $_ -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue }
```

```text
❌ BAD — kill whatever is on 3002/5173/5174 because the turn ended
✅ GOOD — leave the user’s already-running API/admin/client alone
```

- Prefer one-shot checks (`typecheck`, `lint`, `build`) over starting a dev server.
- Leave a process running only if the user asks, or if it was already running when you arrived.
